    basic: 'Early Game: Prioritize revealing your face-down cards quickly by drawing from the stock or strategically taking discards that allow useful replacements. Target high-value cards (face cards, aces if high) for replacement. Favor Kings since they score zero points.',
    intermediate: "Column Control: Watch what cards have been revealed by opponents and in the discard pile. If you see two cards of the same rank, try to acquire the third to complete a zero-scoring column. Discard Management: Remember what's been played; avoid creating a discard pile full of cards that help opponents complete patterns. Position Awareness: Note which of your face-down cards are in the same column as high-value face-up cards, and prioritize replacing those face-down cards.",
    advanced: 'Endgame Prediction: As the round nears completion (when someone has 8-9 face-up cards), calculate which opponent will reveal their final card and when. Block them by refusing to replace certain high-value cards if it helps you more. Strategic Discard Timing: Sometimes hold onto low-value discards to prevent opponents from accessing cards they need. Calculate Opponent Columns: Deduce what face-down cards opponents likely hold based on their play pattern, and avoid giving them opportunities to complete three-of-a-kind columns.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Early Reveals: Reveal high-point cards face-down early to avoid being surprised by high scores late in the round.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Three-of-a-Kind Hunt: If you've seen two cards of the same rank face-up (yours or discarded), immediately pursue the third card aggressively.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Kings are Gold: Always keep Kings if you draw them; they contribute zero points and can anchor your grid.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Endgame Math: Near the end, add up your current cards and estimate if you can win. Sometimes intentionally delaying revealing your last card is strategic if your score is high.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Discard Pile Reading: Pay close attention to the discard pile; it reveals which cards are in play and helps you predict future draws.',
      },
